d_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Predhelt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-15T05:03:27Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T13:51:01Z","body":"I narrowed down the problem to be something with a peripheral I had plugged into my computer via USB hub: a Victrix Pro BFG Controller. I think it has something to do with the MSI / GPU software unintentionally interacting with the controller when the Victrix Control Hub is not open (or is minimized), causing Godot and some other applications to crash or loop on startup. I think this because when I plug the controller into the computer, the MSI Companion asks for permission to make changes to the computer. This could be unrelated to the exact problem, since denying or accepting the request both result in the apps not launching without the Control Hub open.\n\nI also tried using Godot 4.4.1-stable on my laptop and it was working fine with the controller plugged in and the control hub closed, so I believe it is a conflict with a combination of the controller and particular hardware/software (likely something with the GPU) causing certain apps to crash.\n\nI am not sure exactly how to prevent the issue other than disconnecting the Victrix Pro BFG Controller or keeping the Victrix Control Hub open while the controller is plugged in.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2973497958/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3576370119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106971#issuecomment-3576370119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106971","id":3576370119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VKxPH","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VX